-- CONTROL for the row above, and the VALUE is what makes it one: `zmod` gains its
-- own `impl Sizer Int` (`bulk n = n + 7`), so `match(IE, zmod.Sizer Int)` is the
-- singleton {zmod's impl} and `useBulk 3` = 10. `10` is a value ONLY `zmod`'s
-- impl can produce (`amod`'s `weight n = 100` is a different interface entirely
-- and is never reached at this receiver), so the PAIR separates "the reject was
-- removed" from "the wrong impl was selected" -- a verdict-only control could
-- not. It rules out the duller readings of the sibling's reject ("a bare
-- cross-module method occurrence cannot dispatch at all"; "any same-spelled
-- interface in the graph poisons the goal"), each of which predicts a reject
-- here too.
import amod
import zmod.{useBulk}

main = println (useBulk 3)
